  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1132 AM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nBelow normal temperatures will continue Wednesday and into\nThanksgiving Day, with a warming trend beginning Friday.\nTemperatures on Wednesday should be a few degrees higher than\nthose this afternoon given the lesser cloud cover. Another upper\nlevel low remains on track to drop through the Central Plains and\ninto the Mississippi Valley Wednesday into Thanksgiving Day, with\nthe main impact here being an increase in northerly winds\nbeginning Wednesday night, particularly across parts of northeast\nOklahoma and into western Arkansas. The increase in wind speeds\nshould keep temperatures Thanksgiving morning warmer than shown by\nthe NBM initialization and also make conditions during the daytime\nhours Thanksgiving feel worse than the already chilly ambient \ntemperatures would indicate. \n\nSoutherly winds make a return for Friday, with temperatures still\nexpected to warm to above normal levels during the afternoon after\nanother chilly start. The warmer conditions will extend at least\ninto Saturday, with some increased uncertainty entering the \nforecast thereafter. A few models continue to show a frontal\npassage for the middle to latter part of the weekend, leading to a\nreturn to stronger northerly winds, cooler temperatures and some \npotential for showers and thunderstorms. Other data are less \nbullish on the late weekend system but show a stronger one early \nin the following week. Expect the forecast after Saturday to\nchange some as a more likely outcome reveals itself.",
